  "about": "Operator channels the featured-cam watcher scans for live streams (personal fork; server/providers/cctv/featuredChannels.js). A stream found here is queued for review, never shown on the map until a person accepts its position. defaultPlace is offered only when every stream on the channel is at that place, at that precision. Channel ids resolved with channels.list forHandle on 2026-10-16 and checked against the operator's own site where it links one. autoTriage (server/providers/cctv/featuredTriage.js) is the owner's placement rule per channel: a stream is accepted without review only at a site-precision place, or an area one marked campus: true (a bounded campus under about 1 km); accept: 'never' skips the channel's streams (NASA: events at studios); maxPerDay caps the automatic accepts a day (6 by default); locations place streams by titleMatch on a channel whose streams are at several places. Not added: Africam (its site links no channel; @africam does not exist), Smithsonian's National Zoo (its webcams stream on nationalzoo.si.edu, not YouTube), Virtual Telescope Project (@virtualtelescope last uploaded in 2013 and its site links no channel).",
